ion, popular culture, decorative arts, and the natural environment of her native Wilmington, North Carolina. Her dense, kaleidoscopic compositions include images of angels, mythical creatures, watchful faces, and intricate patterns that suggest harmony and transcendence amid hints of an unsettling disquiet. At once evocative and mysterious, these works imagine…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://whitneymedia.org/assets/image/833778/EXME072%20Evans.jpg","sourceURL":"https://whitney.org/exhibitions/the-lost-world","sourceName":"Whitney Museum of American Art","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"cur-the-museum-of-modern-yoko-ono-imagine-peace","title":"Yoko Ono: IMAGINE PEACE","category":"art","venueID":"osm-w278346578","start":"2026-09-03T04:00:00Z","end":"2027-06-01T03:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/MoMa_NY_USA_1.jpg/960px-MoMa_NY_USA_1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","sourceURL":"https://www.moma.org/calendar/exhibitions","sourceName":"The Museum of Modern Art","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"whitney-lichtenstein-1997","title":"Roy Lichtenstein: 1997","category":"art","venueID":"osm-w288749896","start":"2026-09-05T04:00:00Z","end":"2027-06-02T03:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Roy Lichtenstein: 1997 is presented on the Museum’s 3rd floor. This exhibition runs in conjunction with the major exhibition Roy Lichtenstein: Like New, opening October 11 on the Museum’s 5th floor. In 1997, at the age of seventy-three, Roy Lichtenstein (1923–1997) was as innovative and productive as ever. In addition to his studio painting practice, he was working on a variety of adventurous projects, among them two mural commissions, several large-scale sculptures, and a new series of prints. Decades after his paintings inspired by comics and other images of American consumer culture helped usher in the Pop art era, Lichtenstein began to expand his palette of mostly primary colors, adding…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://whitneymedia.org/assets/image/833779/WMAA20998_2019_79_cropped_web.jpg","sourceURL":"https://whitney.org/exhibitions/lichtenstein-1997","sourceName":"Whitney Museum of American Art","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[{"outlet":"The New York Times","title":"Alex Da Corte Takes On Roy Lichtenstein and Marisol","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/28/arts/design/pop-art-dacorte-lichtenstein-marisol.html","date":"2026-10-28"}],"selected":true,"spotNote":{"en":"Pop at its sharpest, and funnier than you remember.","fr":"Le pop art à son plus vif, et plus drôle que dans vos souvenirs.","es":"El pop en su versión más afilada, y más divertido de lo que recuerdas."},"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"artlogic-ny-miles-mcenery-gallery-suzanne-caporael10","title":"SUZANNE CAPORAEL","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n10861418204","start":"2026-09-09T22:00:00Z","end":"2026-10-31T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Suzanne Caporael’s tenth solo exhibition with the Miles McEnery Gallery, Fitting, demonstrates an ongoing interest in the visual manifestation of theoretical concepts. In this series, using the four-color theorem of cartography, the artist fits polyomino shapes into one another. Tertiary colors describe their adjacency and boundaries within the image as a whole. These shapes serve as an organizational syntax, forming a constructive proof that explores the tension between rigid systems and the fluidity of perception.\r\n\r\nAs these polyominoes interlock and tessellate across the canvas, their boundary edges are softened by Caporael’s signature paint handling; the multiple semi-opaque layers…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":null,"sourceURL":"https://www.milesmcenery.com/exhibitions/suzanne-caporael10/","sourceName":"Miles McEnery Gallery","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":false,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"artlogic-ny-miles-mcenery-gallery-roy-dowell4","title":"ROY DOWELL","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n10861418204","start":"2026-09-09T22:00:00Z","end":"2026-10-31T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Roy Dowell’s solo exhibition Evidence to the Contrary, showcases twenty-five new single format works composed of vinyl emulsion on linen over panels. The works are meditations on Dowell’s personal cabinet of curiosities, his memory of objects, and living between Mexico City and Los Angeles. Dowell is drawn to this specific medium because it allows each layer of the painting to remain fully visible. By eliminating the concealment typical of the creative process, the work achieves a transcendence of time. While each work shares the same dimensions at twenty-four by eighteen inches, the only other unifying feature that links them is Dowell’s artistic intent. He approaches the creation of each…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":null,"sourceURL":"https://www.milesmcenery.com/exhibitions/roy-dowell4/","sourceName":"Miles McEnery Gallery","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":false,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"artlogic-ny-miles-mcenery-gallery-isca-greenfield-sanders5","title":"ISCA GREENFIELD-SANDERS","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n10861418204","start":"2026-09-09T22:00:00Z","end":"2026-10-31T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Isca Greenfield-Sanders’ fifth solo exhibition at Miles McEnery Gallery, The Language of Flowers, debuts new mixed media acrylic paintings derived from the rich history of floral paintings. Greenfield-Sanders found inspiration in visits to local and international gardens, botanical illustrations, stained glass, and photogenic drawings. The work of historical women floral painters was of particular interest notably, Clara Peeters, Mary Delaney, and Agnes Northrop. Unlike previous paintings which were based on found imagery, Greenfield-Sanders photographed all her own reference images for this body of work. Borrowing and modernizing the tactics of Renaissance painters, her material process is…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":null,"sourceURL":"https://www.milesmcenery.com/exhibitions/isca-greenfield-sanders5/","sourceName":"Miles McEnery Gallery","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":false,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"artlogic-ny-miles-mcenery-gallery-lucy-williams","title":"LUCY WILLIAMS","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n10861418204","start":"2026-09-09T22:00:00Z","end":"2026-10-31T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"We are delighted to present Lucy Williams’ inaugural solo show, Lucy Williams: Beautiful, Perfect Things, at Miles McEnery Gallery. Williams’ intricate architectural mixed-media collages teeter between realism and abstraction. Heavily inspired by the British modernist movement and Bauhaus architecture,Williams’ scenes build worlds of splendid color, varied textures and an atmospheric sense of light. Each component is carefully conceived, with intentionally sourced materials that allude to historic references, female artist peers, and most recently, to previous works of her own.Williams shared that the works are “speaking to one another.”\r\n\r\nWilliams’ process is thoughtful; consisting of…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":null,"sourceURL":"https://www.milesmcenery.com/exhibitions/lucy-williams/","sourceName":"Miles McEnery Gallery","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"f